orchadOS: the ROS 2 node fills the IMU orientation in the SDK's order.

Upstream: unitreerobotics/unilidar_sdk2 issue #14 (open). LidarImuData::quaternion
is (w, x, y, z): the ROS 1 driver reads it so (unitree_lidar_ros.h) and so does
this node's own imu_initial -> imu transform. The ROS 2 Imu message read it as
(x, y, z, w). The SDK's example.h prints the same array labelled "(x, y, z, w)",
so the order is checked on the bench (README, "L2 sürücüsü").

Made on upstream commit 0e3c51f512e6b8ff60b8c32f160b412cb48445c2 (v2.0.10);
services/kit-recorder/setup/install.sh pins it (UNILIDAR_COMMIT).

diff --git a/unitree_lidar_ros2/src/unitree_lidar_ros2/include/unitree_lidar_ros2.h b/unitree_lidar_ros2/src/unitree_lidar_ros2/include/unitree_lidar_ros2.h
index 29c094c..83b2696 100644
--- a/unitree_lidar_ros2/src/unitree_lidar_ros2/include/unitree_lidar_ros2.h
+++ b/unitree_lidar_ros2/src/unitree_lidar_ros2/include/unitree_lidar_ros2.h
@@ -176,10 +176,12 @@ void UnitreeLidarSDKNode::timer_callback()
             imuMsg.header.frame_id = imu_frame_;
             imuMsg.header.stamp = timestamp;
 
-            imuMsg.orientation.x = imu.quaternion[0];
-            imuMsg.orientation.y = imu.quaternion[1];
-            imuMsg.orientation.z = imu.quaternion[2];
-            imuMsg.orientation.w = imu.quaternion[3];
+            // The SDK's quaternion is (w, x, y, z): as in the ROS 1 driver and
+            // in this node's own imu_initial -> imu transform below.
+            imuMsg.orientation.w = imu.quaternion[0];
+            imuMsg.orientation.x = imu.quaternion[1];
+            imuMsg.orientation.y = imu.quaternion[2];
+            imuMsg.orientation.z = imu.quaternion[3];
 
             imuMsg.angular_velocity.x = imu.angular_velocity[0];
             imuMsg.angular_velocity.y = imu.angular_velocity[1];
